    "done_when": "tests/test_a_foreign_pid_never_reads_dead.py builds, in a temporary crew home, case F (a pointer whose launcher_host is a different host, with a fresh stream plus one commit beyond base) read through list_live then the watcher snapshot, asserting it is not interrupted with dead-pid-with-retained-work; plus case H (a foreign record whose worker.json names a live local pid), asserting it does not read alive with liveness_proven true. It carries three further cases: a local launcher_host with a truly absent pid still emits the retained-work interruption; a foreign record with an exit record still reads process gone through the exit-record route; a fingerprint of the real crew home before versus after shows it untouched. Case F fails at the base revision (logged) and passes at the head. The negative control, in a scratch copy, restores the ungated list_live write; case F fails, with the mutation on the red log's first line and an EXIT= line after pytest's output. The gate is the new test plus tests/test_a_live_run_never_reads_dead.py plus tests/test_stalled_row_names_liveness.py; both arms are recorded as one JSON object each under baseline_suite and after_suite (revision, command, exit_status, one log_path, failure_ids), each log ending in an EXIT= line, with the head arm adding no failing id. ruff check plus ruff format --check on the changed paths add no finding against the base.",
